{
  "ruleId": "DED-DONATION-CASH",
  "_note": "The cash bar: \"Any deduction for a donation over ₹ 2000 shall be allowed only if the payment is made by a mode other than cash\" (s.133(5), p.169) — per donation; one over the limit in cash is allowed nothing, one within it is allowed as any other. A definition (CashPaymentLimit), not a cap, because the excess is not what is disallowed. Old regime only: s.202(2)(a)(xii) excludes Chapter VIII other than ss.124(1), 124(2), 125(2) and 146 (p.227). TY 2026-27 only; the 1961 counterpart, s.80G, is unread (W-075d). rulebook DED-80G-001. D-142.",
